/* --- v0.4: 掉速归因 + 磨损趋势预测 --- */
"Sustained write held steady — no SLC-cache cliff or thermal throttling." = "持续写入保持稳定——没有 SLC 缓存掉速，也没有热降频。";
"Speed stayed within %lld%% of its peak for the whole write. This drive can sustain large transfers at full pace." = "整个写入过程速度始终在峰值的 %lld%% 以内。这块盘能以满速持续传输大文件。";
"Sustained write dropped %lld%% — thermal throttling." = "持续写入下降 %lld%%——热降频所致。";
"Sustained write dropped %lld%% — the SLC write cache filled up." = "持续写入下降 %lld%%——SLC 写入缓存被写满。";
"Temperature stayed moderate (peak %lld°C), so heat isn't the cause. The fast pSLC buffer ran out and writes fell back to slower native NAND at ~%lld MB/s. Normal for the drive — just expect this on transfers larger than the cache." = "温度保持平稳（峰值 %lld°C），所以不是发热问题。高速 pSLC 缓存耗尽，写入回落到较慢的原生 NAND，约 %lld MB/s。这是该盘的正常表现——传输量超过缓存容量时就会出现。";
"Sustained write dropped %lld%% from its peak." = "持续写入较峰值下降 %lld%%。";
"No temperature track for this drive (its enclosure doesn't expose SMART), so NVMeter can't tell thermal throttling from an SLC-cache cliff." = "这块盘没有温度数据（其硬盘盒不暴露 SMART），因此 NVMeter 无法区分是热降频还是 SLC 缓存掉速。";
"The drive warmed %lld°C during the write, peaking at %lld°C, and speed fell to ~%lld MB/s as it throttled. Better cooling (a heatsink or a ventilated enclosure) would help sustain it." = "写入过程中温度升高了 %lld°C，峰值 %lld°C，降频后速度回落到约 %lld MB/s。改善散热（加装散热片或换通风更好的硬盘盒）有助于维持速度。";
"The drive reached %lld°C and throttled to ~%lld MB/s. Better cooling would help sustain it." = "硬盘温度达到 %lld°C 并降频到约 %lld MB/s。改善散热有助于维持速度。";
"At the current rate, wear reaches %lld%% around %@." = "按当前速度，磨损将在 %2$@ 前后达到 %1$lld%%。";
"Now at %lld%%, climbing about %@%% per year over the last %lld days. Most drives keep working past %lld%% — it's the manufacturer's rated endurance, not a cliff." = "当前 %1$lld%%，过去 %3$lld 天里约以每年 %2$@%% 的速度上升。大多数硬盘超过 %4$lld%% 仍可正常工作——这是厂商标称的耐久值，并非寿命终点。";
"Wear is flat — no measurable NAND endurance used over the recorded history." = "磨损保持平稳——在已记录的历史中没有可测量的 NAND 耐久消耗。";
"Holding at %lld%% across %lld days. Light enough use that there's nothing to project — or an Apple SSD, which reports wear only in coarse steps (watch lifetime writes instead)." = "在 %2$lld 天内稳定保持 %1$lld%%。使用强度很低，无从预测——也可能是 Apple SSD，它只以粗粒度报告磨损（请改看累计写入量）。";

/* --- v0.4: USB-SATA 探测阶梯 + 贡献飞轮 --- */
"NVMeter unlocked this enclosure's SMART by probing — it's not in the community database yet." = "NVMeter 通过探测解锁了这个硬盘盒的 SMART——它还不在社区数据库里。";
"Contribute it to the database" = "贡献到数据库";
"Opens a pre-filled GitHub issue with the working -d flags and your enclosure's USB identity so we can add it to NVMeter-drivedb." = "打开预填好的 GitHub issue，附上可用的 -d 参数和硬盘盒的 USB 标识，以便加入 NVMeter-drivedb。";
"Tried every translation mode automatically. For SMART on this drive, connect it through a Thunderbolt enclosure — PCIe pass-through isn't blocked." = "已自动尝试所有翻译模式。要读取这块盘的 SMART，请改用雷雳硬盘盒——PCIe 直通不受限制。";
"NVMeter couldn't confirm a self-test on this drive — it reported no progress and logged no result. This usually means the USB enclosure's bridge chip doesn't pass NVMe self-test commands through. A Thunderbolt enclosure (direct PCIe) is the reliable path; the drive may also self-test fine on Linux/Windows." = "NVMeter 无法确认这块盘的自检——它没有报告任何进度，也没有记录结果。这通常意味着 USB 硬盘盒的桥接芯片不透传 NVMe 自检命令。雷雳硬盘盒（PCIe 直通）是可靠途径；这块盘在 Linux/Windows 上也可能正常自检。";
"This drive's controller rejected the self-test command — it advertises the capability but doesn't actually implement it (a known quirk of some budget NVMe SSDs). Nothing NVMeter can do; this is firmware-side. Live SMART monitoring still works normally." = "这块盘的控制器拒绝了自检命令——它声明支持该能力，但实际并未实现（部分入门级 NVMe SSD 的已知固件毛病）。这是固件层面的问题，NVMeter 无能为力；实时 SMART 监控仍然正常工作。";

